# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WolffMsg web client — build-time configuration
#
# These are read by Vite when the client is BUILT and are baked into the
# output, so nothing secret belongs here. The client holds no secrets of its
# own: keys are generated in the browser and never leave it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the API lives. Leave empty for the normal deployment, where the server
# (or a reverse proxy in front of it) serves this client from the same origin —
# that is the recommended shape, because `SameSite=strict` cookies then do
# their full job.
#
# Set it only when the client is published separately, e.g. to a static host:
#   VITE_API_ORIGIN=https://chat.example.com
# That server must then run with COOKIE_SAMESITE=none, COOKIE_SECURE=true and
# this client's origin in WEB_ORIGIN. See SECURITY.md for what it costs.
#
# Leaving it empty on a static host is also fine: the app asks each visitor
# which server to use.
VITE_API_ORIGIN=

# Sub-path the built client is served from. `/` for a normal deployment,
# `/<repo>/` for a GitHub Pages project site. The Pages workflow sets this
# automatically.
BASE_PATH=/

# Dev only: where `npm run dev` proxies /api and /ws.
VITE_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:4000
